["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/eori", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[Economic Operators Registration and Identification (EORI) number](https://taxation-customs.ec.europa.eu/customs/customs-procedures-import-and-export/customs-operations/economic-operators-registration-and-identification-number-eori_en) is a unique identifier for businesses undertaking customs operations across European Union customs territory, such as import, export, and transit. It consists of an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code followed by a national identifier of up to 15 alphanumeric characters (e.g., `PL1234567890ABCDE`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Dataset/datasetAvailability", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Availability of a dataset.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/VulnAssessmentRelationship", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property", "_:N57ac10b15e3d4774b696b8d0e491f036", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RequirementStatusType/reviewable", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/x509Cert", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A reference to an X.509 certificate as defined in [RFC 5280](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc5280/). The primary media type shall be `application/pkix-cert`. The legacy media types `application/x-x509-ca-cert` and `application/x-x509-user-cert` may be used for backward compatibility, but shall not be used in new implementations. NOTE \u2014 RFC 5280 supersedes earlier X.509 profiles, including RFC 1422. Existing references based on RFC 1422 remain valid.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N17fa5648d31f4cbeafb53d8b98264cae", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/profileConformance", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Dataset/DatasetType/numeric", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "numeric", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasOutput", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The `from` /Build/Build, DefinedProcess or Action element generates each `to` Element as an output.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Dataset/DatasetType/graph", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/VexUnderInvestigationVulnAssessmentRelationship", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Designates elements as products where the impact of a vulnerability is being\ninvestigated.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/ancestorOf", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "ancestorOf", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/bower", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A reference to a Bower package. The package locator format, looks like `package#version`, is defined in the \"install\" section of [Bower API documentation](https://bower.io/docs/api/#install).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/quantity", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty", "globalId", "", ""]
